* The transit pod in the tube by the lab (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our
* own script), retired. The pod (3 6 3) carried creatures between its dock
* by the domed lab and a ledge at the gene lab; since 2026-11-19 the tube is
* walked instead (tube-walk.cos, which also removes the pod and its two
* callers, the world file's). This file now only clears the pieces it made
* in earlier versions (a world saved with them) and keeps the lab powered.
* Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
enum 2 2 214 kill targ next
enum 2 2 215 kill targ next
enum 2 1 143 kill targ next
enum 2 2 219 kill targ next

* The lab starts powered (owner, 2026-11-09). The lab's power switch (3 10
* 11, left of the dock) starts the lab's machines (3 10 8-10) and enables
* the lab console (2 2 21, OV01) (and the pod's dock button, 2 2 22, gone
* now). The first time, it also moves the camera to the lab and shows a
* message, unless the console's OV02 is already 1; we set that first so the
* start is quiet, then press the switch.
enum 2 2 21 setv ov02 1 next
enum 3 10 11 doif ov00 eq 0 mesg writ targ 0 endi next
* A world saved with the power on keeps the generator on (OV00 1), but the
* splicer's console comes back from the world file thinking there is no
* power (its OV01 0), so a press did nothing but open the "no power" window
* (owner, 2026-11-19): the console now takes the generator's state at load.
setv va00 0
enum 3 10 11 setv va00 ov00 next
enum 2 2 21 setv ov01 va00 next

* The dome's power button (owner, 2026-11-19, night: the button on the
* dock's wall that called the pod, "formerly the pod button--turns the
* power on and off in the dome"; the generator on the desk no longer does).
* The pod's button (2 2 22) went with the pod (tube-walk.cos, 0.16.0); a new
* one stands in its place (4564,1464), the game's own picture for it (com_
* frames 36-37, the player's copy), hand only (ATTR 20, hidden from creatures),
* behind creatures. A press starts the generator (3 10 11, its activate 1)
* when the power is off and stops it (its deactivate) when on, through the
* generator's own scripts, so the lab's machines and the splicer's console
* follow as before. The generator itself takes no clicks any more (BHVR 0
* 0) and creatures no longer see it (ATTR 0).
* Its light shows the power (owner, 2026-11-20: "green when the power is
* on, and red when the power is off"): com_ frames 36 (green) and 37 (red),
* picture 0 and 1 from first image 36; a timer every 10 ticks takes the
* generator's state (OV00 1 on), so it is right after a press, at load,
* and whatever else switches the power.
enum 2 2 22 kill targ next
inst new: simp com_ 2 36 1300 0 setv cls2 2 2 22 setv attr 20 bhvr 1 0 pose 1 mvto 4564 1464 tick 10 slow
enum 3 10 11 setv attr 0 bhvr 0 0 next

scrp 2 2 22 1
  doif from eq pntr
    snde ding
    enum 3 10 11
      doif ov00 eq 0
        mesg writ targ 0
      else
        mesg writ targ 2
      endi
    next
  endi
  setv actv 0
endm

scrp 2 2 22 9
  setv var0 0
  enum 3 10 11 setv var0 ov00 next
  doif var0 eq 1 pose 0 else pose 1 endi
endm

scrp 2 2 22 0
  setv var0 0
endm
